# Test: show ping with do-not-fragment over a clamped path reports the MTU
# Spec: spec-probe-do-not-fragment -- user story 1, AC-2, AC-3, AC-5, AC-6 (closed 2026-09-15)
# VALIDATES: an operator runs `show ping <address> size 1500 do-not-fragment`
#            over a path whose middle router clamps its far link to 1400. The
#            probe socket carries IP_MTU_DISCOVER, the router refuses the probe,
#            the kernel queues the ICMP error, and the payload names the router's
#            answer: reply status `too-big`, `next-hop-mtu-reported` true and
#            `next-hop-mtu` 1400, on the reply and on the summary. The
#            `bypass-cache` value gives the same answer because the router, not
#            the cache, refuses it. A 1300-octet DF probe is answered first, so
#            the refusal is the size and never the path.
# PREVENTS: a DF keyword the grammar accepts and the socket never honors, a
#           probe fragmented in silence and answered as if it fit, and a
#           reported MTU dropped by the receive loop as a datagram that is not
#           an echo reply.
#
# The path is three network namespaces joined by veth pairs, built by the
# compiled fixture `plugin/clamped-path` (internal/test/fixture, netlink): the
# daemon runs in the sender namespace, the router forwards with its far link at
# 1400, and the far namespace answers. Building them needs CAP_NET_ADMIN and
# the raw ICMP socket needs CAP_NET_RAW, so the test runs in the QEMU guest as
# root (`./le qemu all-tests`) and skips in the unprivileged merge gate. The
# fixture removes the namespaces when the daemon exits, whatever its exit code.

option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin,net-raw
option=env:var=ze.storage.blob:value=false

tmpfs=probe.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external ping-df-test {
		run "ze-test fixture plugin/ping-do-not-fragment"
		encoder json
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture plugin/clamped-path netns zedf$PORT run ze start probe.conf:timeout=40s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: a DF probe over the clamp reported next-hop-mtu 1400 in both modes, and one under it was answered
reject=stderr:pattern=ZE-OBSERVER-FAIL
reject=stderr:pattern=panic recovered
